      register: "optional '_Register_: <word-family> \u2014 <exemplar words>. Reject <rejected register>.' line, declared once per context (on the context's own anchor or as a glossary preamble), naming the word-family the context's vocabulary is drawn from. It is the target the idiom test (primitives/communicate.md) checks a term against: a term from ambient software/networking/business idiom rather than the declared register is a candidate the writer must replace or justify. Absent a declaration the test falls back to the universal rule \u2014 reject the ambient idiom, prefer the plain word. Enforcement is convention, never mechanism: no gate rules prose idiomatic.",
      slug_retirement: "a term-<slug> id is never repurposed for a different concept \u2014 retire the term and mint a new slug, never rebind",
