    domain_discovery: "domains are DISCOVERED, not declared: cluster the system's entities and components by correlation strength \u2014 shared vocabulary, direct interaction, co-change \u2014 and form a domain from each strongly correlated cluster with weak external coupling. A discovered domain is an abstraction layer that composes with its peers through named seams. The file-level context split (own design.md + CONTEXT.md) is the STRONGEST form and requires a second real vocabulary; below that threshold discovered domains still structure the design document \u2014 its sections, its NN.M disclosure, and its diagrams follow the domain clusters, never an arbitrary outline. Discovery is CONTINUOUS, not creation-only: it runs when a design is created (new-design), when one is derived (sync onboard), and again on every meaningful design update \u2014 a delta that adds, moves, or newly couples components re-asks whether the clusters still hold (small deltas rarely change them; structural deltas and large refactorings must reconsider). A split or merge of domains is itself an intent change, led through the layer like any other. The clustering is PROPOSED by the agent and RULED by the user: domain boundaries are semantic understanding \u2014 how the owner sees the system \u2014 so the agent recommends a granularity with its justification (grilling when the carving is genuinely uncertain), and the user's view decides; under afk the recommendation proceeds and the decision is recorded for review",
