    ownership: {
      design_doc: "the design itself, in three aspects: the single authoritative snapshot of intent (the true source of design information), human-optimized (progressive disclosure, domain structure, reproduction depth), richly presented. Self-sufficient and concise: links a CONTEXT term where a word needs knowing; links an ADR briefly only where a reader would ask why \u2014 never depends on either to state the design",
      context: "semantics \u2014 the canonical definition, one term per anchor, plus every semantic nuance that would clutter the design document; no implementation detail",
      adr: "metadata to the design \u2014 the reasoning, discussion, and history behind one decision per anchor; NEVER contains the design itself, and the design document never depends on it",
      sole_writer_rule: "a sole writer is minted PER KIND of durable authored artifact \u2014 the general form, never a per-repo exception: the design layer's writer is design-write, the system-under-change's writer is work-order. A repo whose durable artifacts include a third kind (e.g. skill definitions, written by write-a-skill) has a third sole writer as an INSTANCE of this rule, not a carve-out. Framing any writer as a 'this-repo exception' leaks the dogfood instance into the generic design."
