      enforced_by: "the conformance probe diffs the system's actual parts against the map: a part present in the system but absent from the map is uncovered drift. review-design walks the map for breadth. Not mechanically enforced by a script yet \u2014 the part-enumeration is judgment \u2014 so the honest tag is convention until a coverage-lint exists.",
      revisitable: "status is not permanent: a standard part that grows non-standard is promoted to captured through the normal design-change path.",
      currency: "the map is created at onboard and MAINTAINED at every reconcile (not only first generation): the conformance probe's breadth sweep reconciles it against the current system each run \u2014 new parts get a status, deleted parts' rows are pruned, standard parts that grew logic are promoted to captured. coder adds a row when a chunk introduces a whole new subsystem. So the map cannot silently rot.",
      patch_accumulation: "DERIVED from git history, never stored: for every captured row, the probe computes the commits touching the row's paths since the row's owning design document last changed (churn-vs-design-age), and reports the ratio on every run exactly like ledger aging \u2014 never silently skipped. A row whose churn reaches the flag threshold while its design stays untouched is a patch-accumulation candidate: the probe emits a proposed (design-change, tracked) finding for the owning unit \u2014 a PROPOSAL routed like any finding, never an auto-route; feature churn under an honest design is the human's call to dismiss. Flag threshold: 5+ commits with zero design movement over the same span; revisable here, cited by the probe and review-design, never redefined locally."
